<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel José Arce</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1787–1847</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel José Arce (1787–1847) was a Salvadoran soldier and politician who became the first president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a> in 1825. Elected after a disputed vote in congress, he drifted towards the Guatemalan conservatives and in 1826 had the liberal Guatemalan head of state <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-barrundia">Juan Barrundia</a> arrested, starting a civil war. The liberal victory under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-morazan">Francisco Morazán</a> in 1829 ended his presidency and sent him into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-jose-arce.jpg" alt="Manuel José Arce" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manuel_Jos%C3%A9_Arce_y_Fagoaga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
